{"id":"hanani","name":"Hanani","aliases":[],"sources":["nave","easton"],"topics":["nave:hanani"],"groups":[],"definition":{"source":"easton","term":"Hanani","text":"God has gratified me, or is gracious. (1.) One of the sons of Heman (1 Chr. 25:4, 25). (2.) A prophet who was sent to rebuke king Asa for entering into a league with Benhadad I., king of Syria, against Judah (2 Chr. 16:1-10). He was probably the father of the prophet Jehu (1 Kings 16:7). (3.) Probably a brother of Nehemiah (Neh. 1:2; 7:2), who reported to him the melancholy condition of Jerusalem. Nehemiah afterwards appointed him to have charge of the city gates."},"lemmas":[{"strong":"H2607","lemma":"חֲנָנִי","xlit":"Chănânîy","gloss":"Chanani, the name of six Israelites","kjv":"Hanani","count":11,"share":1},{"strong":"H3058","lemma":"יֵהוּא","xlit":"Yêhûwʼ","gloss":"Jehu, the name of five Israelites","kjv":"Jehu","count":4,"share":0.36},{"strong":"H1201","lemma":"בַּעְשָׁא","xlit":"Baʻshâʼ","gloss":"Basha, a king of Israel","kjv":"Baasha","count":2,"share":0.18},{"strong":"H2608","lemma":"חֲנַנְיָה","xlit":"Chănanyâh","gloss":"Chananjah, the name of thirteen Israelites","kjv":"Hananiah","count":2,"share":0.18},{"strong":"H3092","lemma":"יְהוֹשָׁפָט","xlit":"Yᵉhôwshâphâṭ","gloss":"Jehoshaphat, the name of six Israelites","kjv":"Jehoshaphat","count":2,"share":0.18}],"verses":["1Kgs.16.1","1Kgs.16.7","1Chr.25.4","1Chr.25.25","2Chr.16.7","2Chr.19.2","2Chr.20.34","Ezra.10.20","Neh.1.2","Neh.7.2","Neh.12.36"],"related":[{"id":"jehu","type":"cooccur","shared":4,"jaccard":0.044,"why":"4 verses are indexed under both"},{"id":"azareel","type":"lexical","strong":"H2607","why":"both lead with חֲנָנִי (H2607)"},{"id":"church-and-state","type":"lexical","strong":"H3058","why":"both lead with יֵהוּא (H3058)"},{"id":"enthusiasm","type":"lexical","strong":"H3058","why":"both lead with יֵהוּא (H3058)"},{"id":"inconsistency","type":"lexical","strong":"H3058","why":"both lead with יֵהוּא (H3058)"},{"id":"intolerance-reli